    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/Bepra/Physics-Teaching-Laboratory-Coordinator,34395": {
      "title": "Physics Teaching Laboratory Coordinator",
      "description": "Physics Teaching Laboratory Coordinator -\r\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Physics Teaching Laboratory Coordinator Te Kura Matū | School of Physical and Chemical Sciences Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays Professional development opportunities Permanent position, 37.5 hours per week Generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) Kia hiwa rā, kia hiwa rā! He hiahia, he pūkenga nōu ki te mahi a te Teaching Laboratory Coordinator ? Nāia te pōwhiri nā Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha kia tono mai i te tūranga nei. Āu Mahi | What You Will Do As our Physics Teaching Laboratory Coordinator, you'll play a key role in delivering an engaging, high-quality practical learning experience for our undergraduate Physics students. You'll take responsibility for the coordination and day-to-day operation of our 100-level Physics teaching laboratories, combining your scientific expertise with laboratory management, teaching support and the development of practical experiments. You'll work alongside Course Coordinators to design, trial and refine experiments that bring lecture content to life. You'll also select, train and schedule demonstrators and teaching assistants, coordinate their workloads and guide them through laboratory experiments, equipment and expected results. You'll provide ongoing support and feedback, preparing them to troubleshoot problems and confidently assist students during laboratory sessions. Behind the scenes, you'll manage laboratory timetabling and changeovers, resolve scheduling conflicts and ensure laboratory activities meet health and safety requirements. You'll also coordinate student assessments and results, and contribute to the School's outreach activities, from delivering NCEA Physics Radioactivity Workshops to participating in KidsFest and Science Summer Camp, helping to inspire the next generation of scientists. Mōu | Who You Are You're a hands-on problem-solver who's just as comfortable troubleshooting scientific equipment as you are guiding a demonstrator or student through their first laboratory session. You take pride in getting the details right and keep a cool head when a dozen things need sorting at once. You're organised, approachable and resourceful, and genuinely enjoy helping students develop the skills and confidence to think like scientists. You'll also bring: An Honours degree in Physics or related subject and at least five years' relevant experience, including substantial experience in a technical environment, preferably within the tertiary education, research or scientific sector. Experience overseeing laboratory operations is desirable. Experience coordinating team workflows and training. Strong technical expertise, including developing, testing and troubleshooting scientific equipment. A sound understanding of laboratory health and safety requirements, including radiation safety. Excellent communication and organisational skills, with a collaborative approach and commitment to fostering a positive and inclusive learning environment. Experience in computer interfacing to scientific equipment would be an advantage. Previous experience coordinating or delivering laboratory sessions or tutorials would be an advantage but is not essential. You'll also hold, or be willing and eligible to obtain, the relevant First Aid Certificate and ionising radiation use licence, with support from the School. Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With Te Kura Matū | School of Physical and Chemical Sciences is one of the largest Schools at the University of Canterbury, bringing together a diverse community of academic, technical and professional staff across disciplines including Physics, Astronomy, Chemistry and Biochemistry. Our School offers a stimulating and collaborative environment, with excellent teaching and research facilities and a strong commitment to scientific discovery and teaching excellence. You'll be part of a supportive community where scientific expertise, innovation and collaboration are central to what we do. You'll work closely with Physics Course Coordinators, academic and technical staff, and the demonstrators and teaching assistants who support our undergraduate laboratory courses. You'll also collaborate with colleagues across the School, contributing to outreach and engagement activities that connect our science with schools and the wider community. As part of our team, you'll have the opportunity to contribute to a School that is passionate about advancing scientific knowledge and inspiring curiosity in the next generation of scientists. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) professional development opportunities supportive working environment a wide range of retail discounts across shopping, entertainment and travel on-campus staff discounts living in revitalised Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa New Zealand a unique working environment in a beautiful campus with access to UC facilities such as UC RecCentre and Staff Club at discounted rates plus onsite cafés and eateries, and more. For more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ The closing date for this position is: 10 th November 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note, applications will be reviewed after the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted via our careers website and should include a cover letter and resume. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz Position enquiries can be directed to the Head of School, Professor Roger Reeves ( spcshos@canterbury.ac.nz ) using the subject line ‘ Physics Teaching Lab Coordinator ’. You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency to be considered for this role. Please note, this is an onsite position. Job Details Reference # 34395 Posted on 27 Oct 2026 Closes on 10 Nov 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Education & Training, Science & Technology, Technician Job level(s) Experienced Work type(s) Continuing (Permanent) full-time More details (document) PD Teaching Laboratory Coordinator.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 30 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/ZoVpa/Lecturer-Teaching-and-Administration-Engineering-Management-Programmes,34100": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Teaching and Administration)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Teaching and Administration)  - Engineering Management Programmes -\r\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Lecturer (Teaching and Administration)  - Engineering Management Programmes Te Tari Pūhanga Hangarau | Electrical and Computer Engineering Department Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand Permanent position, 37.5 hours per week Kia hiwa rā, kia hiwa rā! He hiahia, he pūkenga nōu ki te mahi a te Pūkenga ? Nāia te pōwhiri nā Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha kia tono mai i te tūranga nei. Āu Mahi | What You Will Do Te Tari Pūhanga Hangarau The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering has an opportunity for a Lecturer (Teaching and Administration), focussing on the Engineering Management Programmes. We invite applications for a continuing Lecturer (Teaching and Administration) position. The appointee will play an important role in the design, coordination and delivery of postgraduate engineering management and project management courses. The appointee will: Coordinate undergraduate and postgraduate courses, with a particular focus on postgraduate courses in engineering management and project management. Design, develop, and deliver inclusive, engaging, and industry-relevant online and face to face learning experiences that support student success, retention, and professional growth. Foster a vibrant and supportive learning community for a diverse student cohort, including domestic and international students, through effective online engagement and responsive student support. Facilitate high-quality course delivery across online and, where required, face-to-face teaching environments, demonstrating flexibility, adaptability, and a commitment to student-centred learning. Contribute to programme administration, course coordination, assessment moderation, curriculum development, quality assurance, student advising, and service within the Department, Faculty, and University. To be successful in this role, you will have excellent teaching, communication, and collaboration skills, together with experience designing and delivering high-quality learning experiences that engage and support diverse learners. Mōu | Who You Are To be successful in this position you will ideally have the following: PhD (NZQA Level 10) in engineering management, project management, or a PhD in a related discipline with relevant work experience demonstrated understanding of, and experience in, delivering effective teaching methods that enable a wide range of learners to succeed, including online and face to face delivery evidence of reflective learning and continuous professional development a willingness to learn about bicultural and multicultural issues in Aotearoa New Zealand society, including a commitment to the principles of Te Tiriti o Waitangi | The Treaty of Waitangi, and display a willingness to engage professionally with equity and diversity. Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With You will be based within Te Tari Pūhanga Hangarau | Electrical & Computer Engineering and will work collaboratively with Tuihono UC | UC Online, Te Kaupeka Pūhanga | Faculty of Engineering, Departments and Schools across UC, and external stakeholders, including industry bodies and employers. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. We offer a range of benefits, for more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc . ( For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ ) The closing date for this position is: Friday 6 November 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note applications will be reviewed after the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted on our careers website and should include the following: a cover letter which includes a 1-page statement outlining your teaching philosophy and experience a CV which includes details of your geological interests and teaching experience. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz This position is open only to applicants who have the legal right to work in New Zealand. You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency to be considered for this role. Overseas applicants who do not currently hold work rights in New Zealand will not be considered. This role sits within the Academic Staff, Associated Staff and Support Staff Collective Agreement and the following base salary scale applies: $100,776 - $123,687. Please note, this is an onsite position. #LI-DNI Job Details Reference # 34100 Posted on 27 Oct 2026 Closes on 06 Nov 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Engineering Job level(s) Academic Work type(s) Continuing (Permanent) full-time More details (document) Lecturer (Teaching and Administration) PD.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 30 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/dVupa/Customer-Experience-Representative,33972": {
      "title": "Customer Experience Representative",
      "description": "Customer Experience Representative -\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Customer Experience Representative UC RecCentre Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand Up to 3 permanent part-time positions available Generous annual leave provisions and professional development opportunities Salary, $55,880 – $64,628 p.a. pro-rata, based on skills and experience We have three permanent part-time shift patterns available: Group A: 20 hours a week | Monday 12pm–4pm; Tuesday–Friday 9:30am–1:30pm Group B : 20.5 hours a week |Tuesday & Wednesday 12pm–4pm; Friday 3:15pm–7:15pm; Saturday & Sunday 8:45am–1pm Group C: 17 hours a week |Friday 12pm–9pm; Saturday & Sunday 12:45pm–5pm Kia hiwa rā, kia hiwa rā! He hiahia, he pūkenga nōu ki te mahi a te Customer Experience Representative? Nāia te pōwhiri nā Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha kia tono mai i te tūranga nei. Āu Mahi | What You Will Do As a Customer Experience Representative, you will be the welcoming face of the UC RecCentre, delivering exceptional service to students, staff, and the wider community. This is a hands-on, people-focused role within a thriving student environment, where our primary focus is supporting the health and wellbeing of our students through positive, engaging experiences. You will: Provide a professional and friendly front-of-house experience, acting as the first point of contact for all visitors Manage reception operations including check-ins, ID verification, bookings, and enquiries (in person, phone, and email) Support facility operations by issuing equipment, managing locker hire, and maintaining safe and tidy spaces (including gym floor upkeep) Process memberships, retail sales, and payments accurately, while providing clear information on services and options Maintain and update membership and booking systems, ensuring records are accurate and up to date Provide general administrative support including data entry, filing, stock management, and coordination of basic office needs Contribute to a positive, safe, and inclusive environment aligned with UC’s values and commitment to wellbeing Mōu | Who You Are You are energetic, approachable, and thrive in a customer-facing environment. You enjoy being part of a team, take pride in maintaining high standards, and are confident managing a variety of tasks in a busy setting.You will bring: 1–2 years’ experience in a reception, customer service, or administrative role (sport/recreation environment advantageous) A strong customer focus with excellent communication and interpersonal skills Proven ability to multitask and prioritise in a fast-paced environment Sound problem-solving skills and a high level of attention to detail Confidence using computer systems, databases, and standard office tools A proactive attitude and willingness to support both front-of-house and operational tasks (including light cleaning and facility upkeep) An understanding of, or willingness to engage with, Te Ao Māori, tikanga, and te reo Māori Alignment with UC’s values of manaakitanga, whanaungatanga, and tiakitanga Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With You will work as part of the UC Recreation and Sport team, collaborating closely with colleagues to deliver a high-quality experience for all RecCentre users. You will engage daily with students, staff, members, and visitors, contributing to a vibrant and inclusive campus environment. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. UC’s Benefits approach is shaped by Ngā Uara | Our Values Whanaungatanga, Tiakitanga, and Manaakitanga. They are designed to be relevant, support and inspire our people, they include: 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays UC Parental Leave (up to 9 weeks paid) + 26 weeks Government paid parental leave and onsite childcare facility generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) flexible working arrangements professional development and study opportunities supportive working environment a wide range of retail discounts across shopping, entertainment and travel on-campus staff discounts including UC RecCentre living in revitalised Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa New Zealand a unique working environment in a beautiful campus with access to UC facilities such as UC RecCentre and Staff Club at discounted rates plus onsite cafés and eateries, and more. For more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ The closing date for this position is: 8 November 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note applications will be reviewed after the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted via our careers website and should include a cover letter and resume. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency to be considered for this role. Please note, this is an onsite position. Job Details Reference # 33972 Posted on 23 Oct 2026 Closes on 08 Nov 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Administration, Sports Job level(s) Entry/Graduate Work type(s) Continuing (Permanent) part-time More details (document) Customer Experience Representative PD.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 30 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
