    "https://jobs.canterbury.ac.nz/jobdetails/ajid/Ji5sa/Senior-Tutor-MMT,34497": {
      "title": "Senior Tutor, MMT",
      "description": "Senior Tutor, MMT -\n        University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Sign in Search jobs Search Show all jobs Keyword or Job Code Locations Any Work type Any Expertise Any show advanced Search Senior Tutor, MMT Management, Marketing and Tourism | UC Business School Located in Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa | New Zealand 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays Professional development opportunities Permanent position, 37.5 hours per week Kia hiwa rā, kia hiwa rā! He hiahia, he pūkenga nōu ki te mahi a te Senior Tutor ? Nāia te pōwhiri nā Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha kia tono mai i te tūranga nei. Āu Mahi | What You Will Do As a senior Tutor, you will contribute to a stimulating, research informed learning environment that supports students to achieve their academic potential. You will deliver engaging, high-quality tutoring, coordinate assessment and feedback, engage with industry, manage a LEARN/Moodle site, and support the ongoing development of courses and programmes. You will also contribute to the wider academic community through student support, quality assurance, university initiatives and collaborative activities that strengthen UC’s teaching and learning environment. Please note that this position does not involve a research component. Part-time applications are encouraged and you must be eligible to work in New Zealand. Mōu | Who You Are You are a knowledgeable and engaging tutor with expertise in your discipline and a commitment to helping students succeed. You bring a reflective approach to teaching, value inclusive learning environments and are motivated to contribute to the wider academic community. You will also be able to demonstrate experience in: Using high-quality written and verbal communication skills, including in cross-cultural communication Ability to manage relationships with external and internal stakeholders Attention to detail; being highly organised and reliable Delivering high-quality tutoring Engaging with a diverse student body Showing a high level of compassion, initiative, and decisiveness Fostering a collaborative environment Working within a university system Promoting and using bicultural competence Supporting students through accessible advice, mentoring and academic guidance. Promoting a positive and inclusive work environment, which aligns with UC's values and culture We also require you to have a Master’s Degree (NZQA Level 9) Mahi Ngātahi | Who You Will Work With You will work collaboratively with the Head of Department/School, the MGMT 100 team, the Master of Business Management coordinator and academic colleagues and the wider University community to deliver high quality tutoring, to support students and to contribute to departmental and university objectives. Ngā Painga o UC | Why UC At UC, being part of our team means more than just a job. We are committed to supporting our kaimahi | staff’s career and wellbeing with benefits designed to help our kaimahi grow and feel connected, supported and valued. 5 weeks annual leave +5 days university holidays generous employer contribution to superannuation (up to 6.75%) flexible working arrangements professional development opportunities supportive working environment a wide range of retail discounts across shopping, entertainment and travel on-campus staff discounts living in revitalised Ōtautahi | Christchurch, Aotearoa New Zealand a unique working environment in a beautiful campus with access to UC facilities such as UC RecCentre and Staff Club at discounted rates plus onsite cafés and eateries, and more. For more information, please visit us: https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/about-uc/work-at-uc/benefits-working-uc For more information about Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha | University of Canterbury, please visit https://www.canterbury.ac.nz/ The closing date for this position is: 3 November 2026 (midnight, NZ time) Please note, applications will be reviewed as they are received, and interviews may take place before the close date. Pēhea te tono mai | How You Apply Applications for this position must be submitted via our careers website and should include a cover letter and resume. Please note, we do not accept applications by email, however we are happy to answer your queries in relation to the application process, please forward these to WorkatUC@canterbury.ac.nz You must have Aotearoa New Zealand or Australian citizenship/permanent residency to be considered for this role. Please note, this is an onsite position. Job Details Reference # 34497 Posted on 20 Oct 2026 Closes on 03 Nov 2026 23:55 Location(s) Christchurch Expertise Lecturer Job level(s) Academic Work type(s) Continuing (Permanent) full-time More details (document) Senior Tutor PD.pdf Position description 1 Position description 2 Position description 3 Position description 4 Print Apply © University of Canterbury | Te Whare Wānanga o Waitaha Agency sign in Powered by SnapHire | Privacy policy 30 This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your Administrator for further assistance. Loading . . ."
